# instance/config/sources.yml — the personal-sensing SOURCE binding (example).
#
# This file selects which PersonalSource adapter framework CORE observes the
# captain's world through. Copy it to `instance/config/sources.yml` and edit the
# `adapter:` line to bind a real source. It is DATA the instance owns —
# framework/ never names an adapter statically; the resolver
# (`framework.sources.get_source()`) reads THIS file and dynamically imports it.
#
# ── Contract ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   adapter: "<module>:<Class>"
#     <module>  a Python module importable once `instance/flavor-a/` is on
#               sys.path (the resolver adds that dir). The module lives under the
#               instance/flavor-a tree; a module resolving OUTSIDE it is refused.
#     <Class>   a zero-arg class in that module implementing the
#               framework.sources.base.PersonalSource Protocol.
#
# ── Fail-closed default ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   ABSENT / malformed / unparseable / unimportable  ⇒  NullPersonalSource:
#   every gather returns thin honest empties, read_note raises, nothing crashes
#   and no other deployment's data can leak. A clean-room / Flavor-B box simply
#   ships no sources.yml (or binds its own org source) and framework runs with
#   no ~/.screenpipe, no vault.
#
# ── Flavor-A binding (this deployment, once SRC-1 lands the adapter) ───────────
# The screenpipe brain adapter — the re-homed BrainAdapter body + acting surface
# that owns ALL screenpipe imports and paths (spec §4.5). Uncomment to bind:
#
# adapter: flavor_a.screenpipe_source:ScreenpipeSource
